From 6453bc04358a3933028606997562bd60e910541a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:56:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add canonical R^2 module, AST-anchored migration script and
 policy tests

hypatiax/core/r2_canonical.py: one R^2 policy shared with LLM-HypatiaX-Hybrid
(constant target -> nan, failed prediction -> -inf, relative tolerance for
tiny-scale targets) plus the benchmark guards the old scorers had
(|pred|>1e100 and R^2<-100 -> -inf). The legacy sign-flip credit ("FIX 1") is
no longer applied by default; HYPATIAX_R2_SIGN_FLIP=1 restores it.

scripts/migrate_r2_repro.py: rewrites _safe_r2 (exp1_ablation, _v2, _pca) and
_far_r2 (_v2, _pca, extrap_r2_far) by function name via ast, preserving each
function's return contract. Dry-run by default, idempotent, parse-checked.
Located by name rather than line number because working trees have drifted
from master.

test_r2_policy.py: policy tests, migration mechanics, a checklist test that
fails until the script has been applied, and a ratchet that stops new ss_tot
copies appearing (baseline r2_legacy_baseline.json may only shrink).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
